Lepidocrocite (FeOOH) crystallizes in the orthorhombic system with the space group symbol **Pnma** (international number **62**). The structure consists of layers of edge-sharing FeO₆ octahedra with OH⁻ and O²⁻ groups, characteristic of the lepidocrocite-type structure.  
SMILES: [Fe](O)(O)=O (for FeOOH molecular unit);  
Molecular formula: FeOOH.
